From: meta-st-odyssey <build@local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 01:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: stm32mp157c-odyssey: add OP-TEE TEE client node

U-Boot's stm32mp_bsec driver only uses the OP-TEE-mediated PTA_BSEC
path when it can find a bound TEE client (priv->tee); otherwise it
falls back to the legacy raw stm32_smc(STM32_SMC_BSEC, ...) call.
Without a "linaro,optee-tz" firmware/optee node in this board's own
devicetree, U-Boot's TEE probe never finds the running OP-TEE
instance, so every BSEC access (MAC address from OTP, board ID, etc.)
takes the legacy path - which fails once OP-TEE has taken exclusive
ownership of BSEC in this secure boot flow:

    stm32_smc: Failed to exec svc=82001003 op=1 in secure mode (err = -1)
    Error: ethernet@5800a000 address not set.
    No ethernet found.

ST's own DK1/DK2/ED1 boards get this node via their -scmi.dtsi
overlays (e.g. stm32mp157c-dk2-scmi.dtsi); this board never had one.
Add just the TEE client node itself, not the separate SCMI-over-OP-TEE
clock/reset transport those overlays also carry alongside it - U-Boot
doesn't touch any of the peripherals that transport would reparent.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [out-of-tree board]

--- a/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp157c-odyssey.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp157c-odyssey.dts
@@ -31,6 +31,25 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	/* U-Boot's own BSEC (OTP) access needs a TEE client session to
+	 * OP-TEE's PTA_BSEC - without this node U-Boot's TEE probe never
+	 * finds OP-TEE, so every BSEC read/write (MAC address, board ID,
+	 * etc.) falls through to the legacy raw-SMC path, which fails
+	 * once OP-TEE has taken exclusive ownership of BSEC:
+	 *   stm32_smc: Failed to exec svc=82001003 op=1 in secure mode (err = -1)
+	 * ST's own DK1/DK2/ED1 boards get this via their -scmi.dtsi
+	 * overlays; this board never had one. Just the TEE client node is
+	 * needed here (not the separate SCMI-over-OP-TEE clock/reset
+	 * transport those overlays also carry - U-Boot doesn't touch any
+	 * of the peripherals that would reparent to). */
+	firmware {
+		optee: optee {
+			compatible = "linaro,optee-tz";
+			method = "smc";
+			interrupt-parent = <&intc>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_PPI 15 (GIC_CPU_MASK_SIMPLE(2) | IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW)>;
+		};
+	};
 };
 
 &adc {
